.TH "FWD DIFF" "1" "2026-08-16" "fwdit" "fwd diff Manual"
.SH NAME
fwd\-diff \- Compare local and remote content with Git-style output:
exit 0 if identical, 1 if different, and 2 on errors.
.SH HOMEPAGE
\fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd\fP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd diff
[OPTIONS] [target] [path]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Compare local and remote content with Git-style output: exit 0 if
identical, 1 if different, and 2 on errors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-q,\fP \-\-quiet
Print no diff; communicate identical/different/error through exit status only.
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-gitignored\fP
Also compare Git-ignored content, while retaining .fwdignore and
configured sync exclusions.
.TP
\fB\-\-include\-unsynced\fP
Compare all ordinarily unsynced content; .git and permanent OS metadata
exclusions still apply.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0\fP means the synchronized trees match, \fB1\fP means they differ,
and \fB2\fP means comparison failed.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd/issues\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfwd\fP(1)
